This is a known .NET 10 breaking change. Android's `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` was deprecated (API 30), and .NET 10 MAUI adopted **edge-to-edge** rendering by default, which ignores the old resize mode.

### The Fix: React to IME WindowInsets

In your Android platform code (e.g., `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`):

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.Compatibility;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        // Listen for keyboard (IME) insets and adjust padding
        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(
            Window!.DecorView.FindViewById(Android.Resource.Id.Content)!,
            new KeyboardInsetsListener());
    }

    private class KeyboardInsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

            // Use the larger of IME or nav bar bottom inset
            int bottom = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom);
            v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottom);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

Also make sure your `AndroidManifest.xml` still has:

```xml
<activity android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize" ... />
```

### Why this works

- **Edge-to-edge** means your app draws behind system bars and the keyboard. The OS no longer auto-resizes your window.
- `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` gives you the **keyboard height**. You apply it as bottom padding so your input bar slides up above the keyboard.
- When the keyboard closes, `imeInsets.Bottom` returns to `0` and the padding resets.

### iOS

On iOS this isn't needed — MAUI's `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` (enabled by default since .NET 8) handles it automatically. If you disabled it, re-enable with:

```csharp
KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Connect();
```
